WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.223 --> 00:00:01.056
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.056 --> 00:00:03.430
- [Narrator] This is the
Gooty Sapphire tarantula,

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:06.580
also known as the Poecilotheria metallica.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:08.240
Their exotic blue color comes from

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.990
tiny hairs that line their bodies,

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.660
making the Gooty Sapphire one of

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.693
the most beautiful species
of tarantula in the world.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.100
The Gooty Sapphire tarantula lives

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.330
in the forest of East Gooty,
India, hence their name.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.910
They are very quick and can defend

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.673
themselves if they feel threatened.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.440
They are extremely venomous.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.920
One bite from them can pack a huge punch,

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:37.070
causing humans excruciating
pain that can last over a week.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.180
The Gooty Sapphire tarantula is

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.170
classified as critically endangered

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.920
because they only live
in a single small area,

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.310
which is now being harvested for firewood,

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:49.250
leading to the loss of their only habitat.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.413
This is the Gooty Sapphire tarantula.

00:00:56.085 --> 00:00:58.835
(dramatic music)

